# PLAN-1078 — 普通 AV 语言基线：表达式与短路（语言共享语料第一份）

The first canonical file of the feature-organized language corpus. Every
case carries ONE Auto source; AV / AC-native / legacy-reference checks share
the same source bytes and record their own real results. The `av` check runs
the ordinary AV language chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`, Auto profile);
it never falls back to the old VM.

The `av` probes require byte-exact dual streams; an OMITTED stdout/stderr
paragraph is loaded as an expected zero-byte stream (PLAN-1078 user ruling),
so empty-stream paragraphs are dropped here. An actually emitted byte —
including a lone newline — still fails the check.

## Case: baseline-value
id: "av.parity.1078.baseline-value"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1078", "basics"]
links: ["PLAN-1078", "PLAN-1002"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn main() int { return 2 + 3 * 4 }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 14

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:14
```

### Probe ac-native
recipe: "ac-aac-gen1/native-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
exit: 14

### VM result
#ignore
check-id: "legacy-reference"
final-newline: false

```text
14
```

### Notes

`av.parity.1078.baseline-value` keeps the planned 1078 id (identical Auto
source to `ace.m1.b01`); the AV check runs the ordinary language chain. The
ac-native check is the PLAN-1053 Gen1 takeover: the same source runs through
the whole-subject Auto compiler (mir) -> 1051 bridge service -> parent-side
link -> the real PE, judged on the corpus exit oracle in the
`case-aac-gen1-language-parity` target view (target `gen1`). The
legacy-reference check keeps its AV-phase `#ignore` marker.

## Case: short-circuit
id: "av.parity.1078.short-circuit"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1078", "basics"]
links: ["PLAN-1078"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn explode() bool { fail("must-not-run") }
fn main() int {
 if false && explode() { return 0 }
 if true || explode() { return 42 }
 return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:42
```

### Notes

The short-circuit polarity case: `&&`/`||` must never evaluate the guarded
`explode()` call (its `fail` would be a language error). The result 42 proves
both guards short-circuited.

## Case: syntax-neighbor
id: "av.parity.1078.syntax-neighbor"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1078", "basics"]
links: ["PLAN-1078"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn main() int { return (40 + 2 }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
stage: "parse"
code: "source.syntax"

### Notes

The nearest-neighbor syntax rejection: the unbalanced `(` is a parse-stage
diagnostic (`source.syntax`), never a silent any-Err. The diagnostic stage/code
is frozen by PLAN-1078 T-01.
